From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:31:13 +0100
Subject: Add -Z, the settings that enable Proscala's optional behaviours by
 name

Each opt-in patch is enabled by its own flag, `-Z<name>` (`-Zliterate-literals`,
`-Zunion-captures`), in the style of -X and -Y; where a name is not given the
compiler runs upstream's code at every site the patch touches. The flags are
declared in a loop over one registry, `config.Proscala`, which holds each
feature's name, patch and help text; a bare -Z prints the synopsis of them
like -X and -Y do, and an unknown name is rejected like any other option.
Patches test `Proscala.enabled(Proscala.<Feature>)` at their sites.

This is the stream's base: every patch is rebased onto it, so the registry is
edited only here, never in a patch (see doc/zflags/zflags.md on main).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: zflags
